                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently there is no way to configure TLS for the JettyHTTPServerEngineFactory in code. &quot;createJettyHTTPServerEngine&quot; passes &quot;null&quot; through to &quot;getOrCreate&quot; for the TLSServerParameters object and an exception will then be thrown when comparing the protocol of the engine to &quot;https&quot;.<br/>
<br/>
The fix is to add an argument which indexes in to the tlsParametersMap. If found then this will be used to configure TLS.
  </td>
