                <tr id="issuerow13060598" rel="13060598" data-issuekey="CXF-7306" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-7306" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-7306">CXF-7306</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Namespace Prefix for Subcode Value is ignored
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Dave Franken
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Dave Franken
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 31/Mar/17 07:40 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 15/Apr/17 18:21 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.1.10            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-WS Runtime,                     Soap Binding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      From an InInterceptor, I&#39;m throwing a custom (WS-Security related) SoapFault:<br/>
<br/>
{code:java}<br/>
SoapFault fault = new SoapFault(&quot;An error was discovered processing the &lt;wsse:Security&gt; header: No wsse:Security-element found&quot;,<br/>
            SOAPConstants.SOAP_SENDER_FAULT);        fault.setSubCode(new QName(&quot;http://docs.oasis-open.org/wss/2004/01/oasis-200401-wss-wssecurity-secext-1.0.xsd&quot;, &quot;InvalidSecurity&quot;, &quot;wsse&quot;));<br/>
throw fault;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
My expectation is that a fault such as this is generated:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
         &lt;soap:Code&gt;<br/>
            &lt;soap:Value&gt;soap:Sender&lt;/soap:Value&gt;<br/>
            &lt;soap:Subcode&gt;<br/>
               &lt;soap:Value xmlns:*wsse*=&quot;http://docs.oasis-open.org/wss/2004/01/oasis-200401-wss-wssecurity-secext-1.0.xsd&quot;&gt;*wsse*:InvalidSecurity&lt;/soap:Value&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/soap:Subcode&gt;<br/>
         &lt;/soap:Code&gt;<br/>
         &lt;soap:Reason&gt;<br/>
            &lt;soap:Text xml:lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;An error was discovered processing the &amp;lt;wsse:Security&gt; header: No wsse:Security-element found&lt;/soap:Text&gt;<br/>
         &lt;/soap:Reason&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
However, a default namespace prefix is chosen:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
         &lt;soap:Code&gt;<br/>
            &lt;soap:Value&gt;soap:Sender&lt;/soap:Value&gt;<br/>
            &lt;soap:Subcode&gt;<br/>
               &lt;soap:Value xmlns:*ns1*=&quot;http://docs.oasis-open.org/wss/2004/01/oasis-200401-wss-wssecurity-secext-1.0.xsd&quot;&gt;*ns1*:InvalidSecurity&lt;/soap:Value&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/soap:Subcode&gt;<br/>
         &lt;/soap:Code&gt;<br/>
         &lt;soap:Reason&gt;<br/>
            &lt;soap:Text xml:lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;An error was discovered processing the &amp;lt;wsse:Security&gt; header: No wsse:Security-element found&lt;/soap:Text&gt;<br/>
         &lt;/soap:Reason&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
The prefix information is lost somewhere.
  </td>
