</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                ResourceInjector swallows @PostConstruct exceptions
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Frode Austvik
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Frode Austvik
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 07/Apr/17 12:50 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 07/Apr/17 12:50 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.1.9,                     3.1.10            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      JSR-250 section 2.5 about {{@PostConstruct}} says (about the annotated method) &quot;If the method throws an unchecked exception the class MUST NOT be put into service.&quot;<br/>
<br/>
However, ResourceInjector just [logs the exception|https://github.com/apache/cxf/blob/cxf-3.1.10/core/src/main/java/org/apache/cxf/common/injection/ResourceInjector.java#L350] and otherwise ignores it, which makes it impossible to know that the object should not be put into service.<br/>
<br/>
I expected that the unchecked exceptions thrown by my resource classes when initialization fails would simply be let through to the calling code, so I could handle the failure properly (or if I didn&#39;t, the application startup would fail). Instead, the class is put into service as if the exception didn&#39;t happen, which causes further failures later when the class is used.
  </td>
