                <tr id="issuerow13080045" rel="13080045" data-issuekey="CXF-7409" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-7409" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-7409">CXF-7409</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                ServiceConstructionException when adding JAX-RS application ruins existing applications
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Carlos Sierra
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Carlos Sierra
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 15/Jun/17 10:27 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 15/Jun/17 10:34 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.1.10            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      if a new application conflicts with<br/>
an existing one, an Exception:<br/>
<br/>
---<br/>
<br/>
Caused by: org.apache.cxf.service.factory.ServiceConstructionException:<br/>
There is an endpoint already running on /test-application.<br/>
      at<br/>
org.apache.cxf.jaxrs.JAXRSBindingFactory.addListener(JAXRSBindingFactory.java:86)<br/>
<br/>
      at org.apache.cxf.endpoint.ServerImpl.start(ServerImpl.java:123)<br/>
      at<br/>
org.apache.cxf.jaxrs.JAXRSServerFactoryBean.create(JAXRSServerFactoryBean.java:206)<br/>
<br/>
---<br/>
<br/>
is raised, which is expected. The problem is that the already existing<br/>
application ceases to work in the bus.<br/>
<br/>
Following [~sergeyb]&#39;s advice I tried removing <br/>
{code:java}<br/>
server.destroy()<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
from the <br/>
{code:java}<br/>
catch(RuntimeException e) {}<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
block in JAXRSServerFactoryBean&#39;s create method. However there is a comment saying that that invocation is there to prevent leaks. Also, invocations to server.destroy() in other moments don&#39;t affect other existing applications in the bus. <br/>

  </td>
