                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hi, <br/>
I am using cxf 3.0.4-redhat-*, Jboss Fuse 6.2.1 and WSO2 Governance Registry 5.3.0. <br/>
<br/>
I have my WSO2 G-REG up and running. Now I want as my each and every fuse bundle having CXF services (SOAP/REST) should register themselves automatically as soon as they are installed in Fuse and de-register when uninstalled. I used CXF WS-Discovery feature and added a configuration as per documentation http://cxf.apache.org/docs/ws-discovery.html. I have done proper steps, debugged the code, Hello/Bye operations are getting invoked (sometimes using proxyService url https://localhost:9443/services/DiscoveryProxy?wsdl and sometimes soap.udp://239.255.255.250:3702) whenever I install/uninstall my bundle - but the problem is nothing is happening in WSO2 G-REG side - I mean services are getting visible in WSO2 G-REG.<br/>
<br/>
Can someone help me on this?
